CORE
explicit_x_procedural_paths.sv
--top main --bound 4
^\[main\.p1_comb\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p2_nba\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p3_alwayscomb\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p4_wire_nba\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p5_port_nba\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p6_concat\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p7_default\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p7_reset\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p8_port_ff\] .*: REFUTED$
^\[main\.c9_bitcast\] .*: PROVED up to bound 4$
^\[main\.c9_twostate\] .*: PROVED up to bound 4$
^\[main\.c_known\] .*: PROVED up to bound 4$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
An explicit x written to a four-state variable is unconstrained, whether
it reaches the variable through a net or a port (p1, p4, p5, p8) or
directly through a procedural assignment (p2, p3, p6, p7). A two-state
target or an explicit two-state conversion reads 0 (1800-2017 6.12.2).
